         description='Gangaramaya is one of Colombo’s best-known Buddhist temples and remains an active place of worship, learning, and cultural activity. Founded in the late nineteenth century near Beira Lake, it is notable for its blend of Sri Lankan and international Buddhist architectural styles. The grounds contain shrine spaces, a Bodhi tree, religious imagery, and collections of gifts and historic objects assembled over generations. The site is linked with the annual Navam Perahera, an important local cultural procession. Visitors should approach the location as a living religious institution rather than only a museum. Allow time to explore respectfully and, when possible, include nearby Seema Malaka as a second short stop.',
