         description='Independence Memorial Hall stands at Independence Square in Cinnamon Gardens and commemorates Sri Lanka’s independence from British colonial rule in 1948. Its architectural language draws on traditional Kandyan audience halls, with a roof supported by carved stone pillars. The surrounding open space is a familiar place for walking and photography, while the memorial itself provides an introduction to a defining event in modern Sri Lankan history. The monument was completed in 1953, and its setting includes landscaped public grounds that are especially pleasant away from the midday heat. This is an accessible short stop for visitors interested in civic history, architecture, and the national identity of independent Sri Lanka.',
