         description='The National Museum of Colombo is a major repository of Sri Lankan history, archaeology, art, and material culture. Established in 1877, the museum occupies a prominent colonial-era building in Cinnamon Gardens, near Viharamahadevi Park. The collections bring together artefacts connected with ancient kingdoms, craftsmanship, religious life, and the island’s varied historical periods. It is a useful introduction for first-time visitors who want the context behind the monuments they will encounter elsewhere in Colombo. A focused visit can cover selected galleries in well over an hour; enthusiasts may want considerably longer. Opening arrangements, exhibitions, and ticket categories can change, so consult the Department of National Museums before travelling.',
