         description='Sri Kailasanathar Swami Devasthanam, often called Sri Kaileswaram or the Captain’s Garden temple, is a historic Hindu temple in the Maradana area near Colombo Fort. The active place of worship is associated with long-standing Tamil Hindu traditions and is known for colourful sculptural ornament and shrines dedicated to Hindu deities. Visitors can appreciate an important part of Colombo’s multi-religious cultural heritage, especially when viewing the decorated temple architecture. Religious rituals take priority over sightseeing, and the temple commonly closes for part of the middle of the day. This makes accurate timing particularly important in a one-day itinerary. The coordinates here refer to the Captain’s Garden temple, rather than other similarly named kovils elsewhere in Colombo.',
